{
 "cases": [
  {
   "id": "proposed-basic-props-status-not-id",
   "level": "Basic Properties",
   "rule": "fixture rule 5",
   "request": {
    "path": "/access/v1/evaluation",
    "body": {
     "subject": {
      "type": "user",
      "id": "alice"
     },
     "action": {
      "name": "write"
     },
     "resource": {
      "type": "record",
      "id": "record-1",
      "properties": {
       "status": "archived"
      }
     }
    }
   },
   "expect": {
    "status": 200,
    "decision": false
   },
   "why": "c-2-2-4 says the deny is based on properties.status, not on the identifier, but it sends record-2, whose fixture status is already archived. Here the identifier is the active record-1 and only the request property says archived.",
   "mutants": [
    "request properties of subject and resource ignored (stored fixture values only)",
    "stored fixture properties win over request properties",
    "resource status taken from the resource id, not from properties (record-2 = archived)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "proposed-batch-whole-object-override",
   "level": "Batch Properties",
   "rule": "c-3-2-7 (whole-object replacement), fixture rules 2 and 5",
   "request": {
    "path": "/access/v1/evaluations",
    "body": {
     "subject": {
      "type": "user",
      "id": "alice"
     },
     "action": {
      "name": "write"
     },
     "resource": {
      "type": "record",
      "id": "record-2",
      "properties": {
       "status": "archived"
      }
     },
     "evaluations": [
      {
       "resource": {
        "type": "record",
        "id": "record-1"
       }
      }
     ]
    }
   },
   "expect": {
    "status": 200,
    "decisions": [
     true
    ]
   },
   "why": "In c-3-2-7 the overriding resource carries type, id and properties, so a PDP that merges sub-fields gets the same result. Here the override has no properties: whole replacement gives record-1 as identified (rule 2, permit), while sub-field merging keeps the top-level properties.status archived (rule 5, deny).",
   "mutants": [
    "batch defaults merged by sub-field instead of replaced whole"
   ]
  },
